      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m actually curious about food options for acid reflux. What should I eat or avoid?",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To manage acid reflux effectively, it's important to know which foods to eat and which to avoid. Here are some guidelines:\n\n**Foods to Avoid:**\n1. **High-fat and Fried Foods**: Such as french fries, potato chips, and fatty cuts of meat, as they delay stomach emptying and can trigger reflux.\n2. **Spicy Foods**: These can irritate the esophagus and worsen symptoms.\n3. **Citrus Fruits**: Oranges, lemons, limes, and pineapples are acidic and can exacerbate reflux.\n4. **Tomatoes and Garlic**: These can also increase acidity and trigger symptoms.\n5. **Chocolate, Caffeine, and Alcohol**: These relax the lower esophageal sphincter, allowing acid to escape into the esophagus.\n6. **Mint and Carbonated Drinks**: Both can cause reflux symptoms.\n\n**Foods to Eat:**\n1. **Lean Proteins**: Chicken, turkey, fish, and egg whites are easier to digest.\n2. **Non-citrus Fruits**: Apples, bananas, and pears are good options.\n3. **Vegetables**: Especially green vegetables, potatoes",
