      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful! Which specific fruits are considered good for acid reflux? Any favorites I might enjoy?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some fruits good for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For managing acid reflux, some excellent fruit options include:\n\n1. **Bananas**: Low in acidity and easy to digest, they can help protect the stomach lining.\n2. **Melons**: Watermelon, cantaloupe, and honeydew are low in acid and hydrating.\n3. **Apples**: They can help neutralize stomach acid and promote digestion (though you mentioned you don't like apple products).\n4. **Pears**: Similar to apples, they are low in acidity and gentle on the stomach.\n5. **Peaches**: These are also low in acid and can be refreshing.\n\nSince you enjoy a variety of fruits, you might find that incorporating bananas and melons into your snacks or smoothies could be particularly enjoyable while helping with your acid reflux.",
