      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Perfect, I actually love watermelon and apples, so that works for me! Are there any daily habits that can also help with reflux, besides just food?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some good habits to help someone with stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To help manage acid reflux, you can adopt several daily habits in addition to dietary changes. Here are some effective practices:\n\n1. **Eat Smaller Meals**: Instead of large meals, try having smaller portions throughout the day to reduce pressure on your stomach.\n\n2. **Avoid Eating Before Bedtime**: Aim to finish your last meal at least 2-3 hours before lying down to sleep.\n\n3. **Maintain Good Posture**: Sit up straight while eating and remain upright for at least an hour after meals to help digestion.\n\n4. **Elevate Your Head While Sleeping**: Use a wedge pillow or elevate the head of your bed to prevent nighttime reflux.\n\n5. **Stay Hydrated**: Drink plenty of water throughout the day, but avoid large amounts during meals.\n\n6. **Limit Alcohol and Caffeine**: Both can trigger reflux symptoms, so it\u2019s best to reduce or avoid them.\n\n7. **Quit Smoking**: If you smoke, quitting can significantly improve reflux symptoms.\n\nIncorporating these habits can help you manage acid reflux more effectively alongside your diet.",
