    "topic": "1-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense. I tend to eat dinner late and sometimes while slouched on the couch\u2014guess that could be a problem! Is being overweight linked to acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does acid reflux happen? Does acid reflux have a reason?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "Yes, being overweight is indeed linked to acid reflux, or gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD). Excess weight, particularly around the abdomen, increases pressure on the stomach, which can cause stomach contents to flow back into the esophagus, leading to reflux symptoms. Even small amounts of weight gain can increase your risk, even if you are still considered to be within a normal weight range. Therefore, maintaining a healthy weight through diet and exercise can significantly help manage and reduce reflux symptoms. Additionally, adopting habits like eating smaller meals, avoiding late-night dinners, and maintaining an upright posture while eating can further alleviate symptoms.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0009-73-15619:3": 0.4403868019580841,
            "clueweb22-en0035-09-14583:5": 0.26777181029319763,
            "clueweb22-en0023-08-01288:3": 0.23044344782829285,
            "clueweb22-en0040-85-04894:17": 0.004152745008468628
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I eat dinner late at night;",
            "I have gained weight recently because I stopped exercising for the last 6 months;"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "judgment": {
