        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m curious about foods that are good or bad for acid reflux. Can you share some suggestions?",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For managing acid reflux, it's important to know which foods to avoid and which to include in your diet. \n\n**Foods to Avoid:**\n1. **High-Fat Foods**: Fried foods, heavy meats, and full-fat dairy products like butter and cheese can trigger symptoms.\n2. **Spicy Foods**: These can irritate the stomach lining.\n3. **Acidic Fruits**: Citrus fruits (oranges, lemons, grapefruits) and certain other fruits like tomatoes can worsen reflux.\n4. **Carbonated Drinks**: Sodas, including Coca-Cola, are best avoided as they can cause stomach distension.\n\n**Foods to Include:**\n1. **Lean Proteins**: Skinless chicken, fish, and egg whites are good options.\n2. **Alkaline Foods**: Green vegetables, potatoes, and non-citrus fruits like apples and bananas can help neutralize stomach acid.\n3. **Complex Carbohydrates**: Oatmeal, brown rice (in moderation), and quinoa are beneficial.\n4. **Healthy Fats**: While fats can worsen symptoms, healthy fats from sources like avocados and walnuts can be consumed in",
