      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s good to know, thanks! Besides food, what are some daily habits I should try or avoid to help with reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some good habits to help someone with stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To help manage acid reflux, consider adopting the following daily habits:\n\n1. **Eat Smaller Meals**: Opt for four to five smaller meals throughout the day instead of three large ones to reduce stomach pressure.\n\n2. **Avoid Late Meals**: Try to finish eating at least two to three hours before bedtime to allow your stomach to digest food properly before lying down.\n\n3. **Maintain an Upright Posture**: Stay upright for at least two hours after meals. Avoid slouching or lying down, as this can promote reflux.\n\n4. **Wear Loose Clothing**: Avoid tight clothing that can increase pressure on your stomach and exacerbate symptoms.\n\n5. **Elevate Your Head While Sleeping**: Consider raising the head of your bed or using a wedge pillow to leverage gravity and keep acid in the stomach while you sleep.\n\n6. **Limit Trigger Foods and Beverages**: Identify and avoid foods that trigger your reflux, such as spicy foods, caffeine, and alcohol.\n\n7. **Stay Hydrated**: Drink water between meals rather than during meals to prevent overfilling your stomach.\n\n8. **Keep a Food Diary**: Track what you",
