    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m curious about what foods are recommended for acid reflux. Also, what should I avoid eating?",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For managing acid reflux, it\u2019s important to focus on foods that are less likely to trigger symptoms while avoiding common culprits. Foods like watermelon, which you enjoy, are considered GERD-friendly due to their high water content and alkalinity. Other good options include oats, bananas, and non-citrus fruits. On the other hand, you should avoid acidic foods like citrus fruits, tomatoes, and spicy or fried foods, as well as high-fat dairy products and carbonated beverages. Keeping a food diary can help you identify specific triggers unique to you. Eating smaller, more frequent meals and avoiding eating right before bedtime can also help reduce symptoms.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0020-31-05749:4": 23.104400634765625,
            "clueweb22-en0011-83-15566:9": 22.56439971923828
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I want to increase my protein intake.",
            "I like a variety of fruits.",
            "I enjoy apple, kiwi, and watermelon."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s interesting! Glad to hear watermelon is good. Are kiwis and apples also okay for reflux? I eat those pretty often.",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some fruits good for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Kiwis and apples can be a bit tricky when it comes to acid reflux. Apples, especially the sweeter varieties, are generally considered safe for most people with GERD and can even be soothing due to their alkalinity. However, kiwis are more acidic and might trigger symptoms in some individuals. Since you eat these fruits often, it\u2019s a good idea to monitor how your body reacts to them. Keeping a food diary can help you identify if either of these fruits causes discomfort. If you notice any symptoms after eating kiwis, you might want to limit their intake or pair them with less acidic foods to reduce the impact.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0041-22-06879:4": 29.38520050048828
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I enjoy apple, kiwi, and watermelon."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s helpful! I love both apples and kiwis, but I\u2019ll watch for any reaction after eating them. Are there any other fruits that are particularly good or bad for acid reflux? What about things like pomegranate or mango?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some fruits good for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Mangoes are a great choice for acid reflux as they are low in acidity, with a pH close to neutral, making them less likely to trigger symptoms. However, it\u2019s best to enjoy them in moderation and observe how your body reacts. On the other hand, pomegranates are more acidic and may aggravate reflux symptoms for some people. Since you love both fruits, you might want to test them individually and note any reactions. Other fruits that are generally good for acid reflux include melons like watermelon, which you already enjoy, as well as bananas and pears. Avoid highly acidic fruits like citrus, pineapples, and grapes, as they are more likely to cause discomfort.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0026-73-16809:10": 24.78070068359375,
            "clueweb22-en0026-73-16809:11": 21.43779945373535,
