          "text": "To manage acid reflux, it's best to avoid highly acidic fruits such as oranges, lemons, limes, pineapples, and grapefruits, as these can trigger symptoms by increasing stomach acid [clueweb22-en0041-54-06342]. Instead, opt for non-acidic fruits like bananas, melons, cantaloupe, guava, and papaya, which are gentler on your stomach [clueweb22-en0005-41-09262]. Lean proteins such as chicken, turkey, fish, and pork are preferable over fatty meats, which can worsen reflux [clueweb22-en0006-74-09876][clueweb22-en0005-41-09262]. High-fiber foods like oatmeal can help absorb stomach acid and reduce discomfort. Additionally, avoid common triggers like tomato-based products, fried and spicy foods, alcohol, and carbonated drinks. Eating smaller meals and not eating right before bed can also help prevent symptoms [clueweb22-en0011-83-15566].",
