          "text": "To manage acid reflux while dining out, avoid common triggers like fried foods, fatty meats, spicy dishes, tomato-based sauces, onions, garlic, citrus fruits, and carbonated or alcoholic beverages. Instead, look for menu items featuring grilled, baked, or steamed lean proteins (like chicken, turkey, or fish), and choose sides of non-acidic vegetables or salads without acidic dressings. Portion control is important\u2014consider sharing dishes or taking leftovers home to avoid overeating, which can worsen reflux. If you enjoy Italian food, opt for pasta with olive oil or light cream sauces instead of tomato sauce. Always feel free to ask for modifications, such as leaving off onions or spicy ingredients, and drink water or non-carbonated beverages with your meal. Planning ahead and knowing your personal triggers will help you enjoy eating out without discomfort [clueweb22-en0021-78-15884][clueweb22-en0005-44-06345][clueweb22-en0027-23-02870]. Do you want tips for late-night eating with acid reflux?",
