          "user_rubrik": "Why does acid reflux happen? Does acid reflux have a reason?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For late-night eating, it's best to have your last meal at least 3-4 hours before going to bed to allow your stomach to empty and reduce the risk of reflux. Avoid making dinner your largest meal, and steer clear of snacks right before sleep, as even small amounts can trigger acid production. Choose lighter, non-acidic foods like lean proteins, vegetables, and non-citrus fruits. Avoid fried, spicy, or fatty foods, as well as alcohol and carbonated drinks in the evening. Additionally, sleeping on your left side and elevating your upper body can help prevent acid from rising into your esophagus while you sleep. Maintaining a healthy weight and avoiding tight clothing at night can also help reduce symptoms [clueweb22-en0009-09-14479][clueweb22-en0042-16-10146][clueweb22-en0000-42-15341][clueweb22-en0022-51-13319]. Would you like specific meal or snack ideas for late dinners?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0009-09-14479:4": 0.04113143829268602,
            "clueweb22-en0042-16-10146:1": 0.03036576949620428,
            "clueweb22-en0000-42-15341:10": 0.029513888888888888,
            "clueweb22-en0022-51-13319:12": 0.029211087420042643
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I eat dinner late at night.",
            "I eat out regularly.",
            "I want to change my lifestyle."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s really helpful, thanks! Could you tell me why acid reflux even happens in the first place? Does it always have a specific cause? The last answer didn\u2019t cover that.",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does acid reflux happen? Does acid reflux have a reason?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Acid reflux happens when the muscle between your stomach and esophagus (the lower esophageal sphincter) doesn't close properly, allowing stomach acid to flow back up. It can be triggered by diet, lifestyle, certain medical conditions, or sometimes have no clear cause. Are there specific foods or habits you want to ask about regarding acid reflux?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0038-68-03750:0": 0.03796333601933924,
            "clueweb22-en0034-50-07413:2": 0.03200204813108039,
            "clueweb22-en0044-75-01522:1": 0.03076923076923077,
            "clueweb22-en0032-81-17497:2": 0.030679156908665108
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I eat dinner late at night.",
            "I eat out regularly.",
            "I want to change my lifestyle."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that helps! Actually, are there any over-the-counter medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are there any ODC medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For quick relief of acid reflux symptoms, antacids such as Tums, Rolaids, Mylanta, and Maalox are widely available and work by neutralizing stomach acid. H2 receptor blockers, including Pepcid AC (famotidine) and Tagamet (cimetidine), reduce acid production and provide longer-lasting relief. Proton pump inhibitors (PPIs) like Prilosec (omeprazole) and Prevacid (lansoprazole) are also available OTC and are effective for frequent or persistent symptoms by significantly reducing stomach acid production. Side effects of these medications are usually mild but can include headache, diarrhea, or upset stomach. If OTC medications do not provide relief, or if you need them regularly, it's important to consult a healthcare provider for further evaluation and possible prescription options [clueweb22-en0009-46-05873][clueweb22-en0020-48-12159][clueweb22-en0009-09-09722]. Are there any interactions between these medications and other drugs?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0009-46-05873:10": 0.047526999678462675,
