          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks! I actually love watermelon, so that\u2019s good news. What other fruits besides melons and bananas are considered safe for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some fruits good for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "In addition to melons (like watermelon, cantaloupe, and honeydew) and bananas, apples and pears are commonly recommended as safe, non-acidic fruits for people with acid reflux [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-3]. Most berries and stone fruits (such as peaches) are also generally well-tolerated, but it's best to avoid citrus fruits (like oranges, lemons, and grapefruits) and pineapple, as their acidity can trigger symptoms [DOC-2][DOC-4]. Including a variety of these non-citrus fruits in your diet can help you enjoy fruit without worsening acid reflux. Would you like meal or snack ideas featuring these fruits?",
