          "user_rubrik": "Why does acid reflux happen? Does acid reflux have a reason?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When you eat late and then lie down, gravity no longer helps keep food and stomach acid in your stomach. This makes it easier for acid to move up into your esophagus, causing reflux symptoms. Experts recommend waiting at least 2-3 hours after eating before lying down or going to bed to allow your stomach to empty and reduce the risk of nighttime reflux. Large or late meals can also increase stomach pressure, further raising the chance of acid reflux at night. Elevating your head while sleeping and making lunch your largest meal can also help minimize symptoms [clueweb22-en0010-23-06105:4][clueweb22-en0039-65-19861:19][clueweb22-en0000-72-15353:10][clueweb22-en0009-09-14479:4]. Are you interested in more strategies for managing nighttime acid reflux?",
