          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m actually looking to find out which foods are good or bad for acid reflux. Can you tell me some?",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Foods that commonly trigger acid reflux include citrus fruits (like oranges, lemons, and pineapples), tomatoes and tomato-based products, spicy foods, chocolate, caffeinated drinks (such as coffee and soda), peppermint, fried foods, fatty meats, cheese, and carbonated beverages. These foods can increase stomach acidity or relax the lower esophageal sphincter, leading to symptoms like heartburn [clueweb22-en0002-19-16904][clueweb22-en0038-01-07788][clueweb22-en0016-33-07650][clueweb22-en0041-54-06342]. On the other hand, non-citrus fruits (such as bananas, apples, and watermelon), mild vegetables (like lettuce, celery, and sweet peppers), and high-fiber foods are generally considered safe and may help reduce symptoms. While individual triggers can vary, focusing on a diet rich in non-citrus fruits, vegetables, and lean proteins is often recommended for managing acid reflux.",
          "citations": {
