            "I want to change my lifestyle.",
            "I'm a software engineer."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for that breakdown\u2014that makes sense now! As for your question, I\u2019m not totally sure but I think prescription meds might be stronger or used if the OTC stuff doesn\u2019t help, right? Maybe they work differently too, or are tailored if someone\u2019s reflux is more severe? Can you tell me more?",
          "user_rubrik": "How do medication for stomach acid reflux work?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Prescription acid reflux medications are often stronger or higher-dose versions of OTC drugs, and may include additional types like prokinetics or foaming agents for severe or persistent symptoms. Are you interested in non-medication strategies for managing severe acid reflux?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0016-53-08494:9": 0.05580773417080898,
