        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What about snacks for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some fruits good for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For acid reflux-friendly snacks that fit your late-night schedule, protein goals, and fruit preferences, focus on these options:\n\n**Best Snack Choices**\n- **Lean Protein + Complex Carb Combos:** Whole-grain toast with almond or peanut butter (in moderation), hardboiled eggs with a few whole-grain crackers, or hummus with cucumber slices. These support higher protein intake and are less likely to trigger reflux.\n- **Low-Acid Fruits:** Apples, bananas, watermelon, and melons are safe and hydrating. Mango and pomegranate are generally tolerated\u2014enjoy in small amounts and monitor your symptoms.\n- **Dairy:** Low-fat Greek yogurt or cottage cheese (if tolerated) offer protein and are less likely to aggravate reflux than high-fat cheeses.\n- **Nuts:** Almonds or sunflower seeds (small portions) provide protein and healthy fats without excess calories.\n- **Other:** Rice cakes, baked chips, or pretzels (preferably whole grain) are convenient and reflux-friendly.\n\n**What to Avoid**\n- Citrus fruits, chocolate, mint, fried or fatty",
