          "user_utterance": "What foods should I eat for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For acid reflux, especially with your late dinners, weight gain, and desire for higher protein and fruit variety, here\u2019s what works best:\n\n**What to Eat**\n- **Lean Proteins:** Grilled chicken, turkey, fish, tofu, and legumes are reflux-friendly and high in protein. Avoid fried or fatty meats, which worsen reflux and weight gain.\n- **Low-Acid Fruits:** Watermelon, apples, bananas, and melons are safe and hydrating. Mango and pomegranate are generally tolerated, but monitor your symptoms as some tropical fruits can be acidic for sensitive individuals.\n- **Vegetables:** Most are safe except tomatoes, onions, and spicy peppers. Opt for greens, cucumbers, and root vegetables.\n- **Whole Grains:** Oatmeal, brown rice, and barley are filling, high-fiber, and help with weight management.\n- **Nuts (in moderation):** Almonds are alkaline and may help, but limit quantity due to fat content.\n\n**What to Avoid**\n- Citrus fruits, tomatoes, onions, garlic, chocolate, mint, fried foods",
