      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What lifestyle changes can help with acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some good habits to help someone with stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To address acid reflux and align with your goals\u2014late dinners, higher protein, weight management, and fruit variety\u2014focus on these lifestyle changes:\n\n**1. Meal Timing & Size**\n- Eat smaller, more frequent meals. Large meals, especially late at night, increase reflux risk (multiple sources).\n- Finish eating at least 3 hours before lying down or bedtime. This is crucial for late dinners\u2014consider shifting dinner earlier if possible.\n\n**2. Weight Management**\n- Losing even 10\u201320 pounds can significantly reduce reflux (supported by several studies).\n- Combine dietary changes with gradual reintroduction of physical activity.\n\n**3. Food Choices**\n- Prioritize lean proteins (chicken, fish, tofu, legumes) and high-fiber foods (whole grains, vegetables).\n- Enjoy low-acid fruits (apples, bananas, watermelon, melons). Mango and pomegranate are generally tolerated\u2014monitor your symptoms.\n- Avoid high-fat, fried, spicy, or acidic foods (tomatoes, citrus, onions, chocolate, mint, caffeine, alcohol).\n\n**4. Other Habits",
