      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What are some signs or symptoms of acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does acid reflux happen? Does acid reflux have a reason?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "The most common signs and symptoms of acid reflux\u2014especially relevant to your lifestyle and dietary changes\u2014are:\n\n**Core Symptoms**\n- **Heartburn:** Burning sensation in the chest or throat, often after eating or when lying down (especially relevant with late dinners) (clueweb22-en0027-06-12523, clueweb22-en0035-94-06090).\n- **Regurgitation:** Sour or bitter-tasting acid backing up into your throat or mouth; sometimes described as \u201cwet burps\u201d (clueweb22-en0038-94-06355, clueweb22-en0042-54-13250).\n- **Dyspepsia:** General stomach discomfort\u2014burping, bloating, upper abdominal pain, nausea, or feeling overly full after meals (clueweb22-en0042-54-13250, clueweb22-en0017-96-03792).\n- **Chest pain:** Can mimic heart pain but is related to acid reflux, especially after meals or when lying down (clueweb22-en0038-",
