          "user_utterance": "What natural remedies are effective for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are there any ODC medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "The most effective natural remedies for acid reflux\u2014tailored to your late dinners, protein goals, weight management, and love of fruit\u2014are:\n\n**1. Low-Acid Fruits**  \n- Bananas, apples, watermelon, cantaloupe, and honeydew are gentle on the stomach and can help prevent reflux (multiple sources). Bananas and apples, in particular, have natural antacid properties.  \n- Mango and pomegranate are generally tolerated, but monitor your symptoms as some tropical fruits can be acidic for sensitive individuals.\n\n**2. Simple Home Remedies**  \n- **Baking soda:** 1 tsp in 8 oz water can quickly neutralize stomach acid. Use only occasionally (no more than 7 times/day, not for more than a week) to avoid side effects.\n- **Honey:** A spoonful may soothe the esophagus and reduce symptoms.\n- **Chewing gum (not mint):** Increases saliva, helping clear acid from the esophagus.\n\n**3. Herbal and Lifestyle Approaches**  \n- **Aloe vera juice:** Can soothe the digestive tract.",
