          "text": "For over-the-counter (OTC) relief of acid reflux\u2014especially given your late dinners, weight management goals, and desire for flexibility\u2014here\u2019s what works best:\n\n**1. Antacids**  \n- **Best for:** Fast, short-term relief after occasional symptoms (e.g., after a late meal).  \n- **Examples:** Tums, Maalox, Mylanta, Rennies.  \n- **How they work:** Neutralize stomach acid quickly.  \n- **Fit for you:** Safe for occasional use, but not a long-term solution if you have frequent symptoms.\n\n**2. Alginates**  \n- **Best for:** Preventing acid from reaching the esophagus, especially after eating.  \n- **Examples:** Gaviscon.  \n- **How they work:** Form a protective gel \u201craft\u201d on top of stomach contents.\n\n**3. H2 Blockers**  \n- **Best for:** Longer-lasting relief (up to 12 hours), mild to moderate symptoms.  \n- **Examples:** Famotidine (Pepcid), Cimetidine (",
