        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That helps. What about mangoes or pomegranates? I really enjoy those, especially since my trip to Brazil last summer. Are they safe for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some fruits good for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Mangoes are generally considered safe for acid reflux as they are close to neutral on the pH scale, making them less likely to worsen symptoms. However, pomegranates are more acidic and may trigger or exacerbate acid reflux. If you enjoy mangoes, you can consume them in moderation, but it's best to avoid or limit pomegranates if you experience acid reflux. As with any food, it's essential to monitor your body's response and adjust your diet accordingly. Enjoy your mangoes, but be cautious with pomegranates.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0026-73-16809:5": 5.68565559387207,
            "clueweb22-en0026-73-16809:6": 5.497569561004639,
            "clueweb22-en0026-73-16809:0": 5.06022834777832,
            "clueweb22-en0026-73-16809:10": 4.46022891998291,
