          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it, thanks! I\u2019ll stick with mangoes and skip pomegranates for now. Are there certain eating habits besides fruit choice that can help reduce acid reflux, especially since I eat dinner late?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some fruits good for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Eating habits play a significant role in managing acid reflux. To reduce symptoms, it's recommended to avoid eating at least three hours before bedtime, as lying down after a meal can worsen reflux. Additionally, wearing loose-fitting clothes, especially around the stomach area, can help alleviate pressure and discomfort. You may also want to consider eating smaller, more frequent meals throughout the day to ease digestion and reduce symptoms. By making these adjustments, you can help minimize acid reflux discomfort, especially when eating dinner late.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0044-72-05971:1": 5.977960586547852,
            "clueweb22-en0027-11-19840:5": 4.750515937805176,
            "clueweb22-en0013-66-13847:14": 4.741585731506348,
