          "text": "For preventing acid reflux, consider eating mild veggies like lettuce and celery, as well as low-acid fruits such as watermelon, cantaloupe, and honeydew. Whole grains like brown rice, oatmeal, and whole-grain breads are also beneficial. On the other hand, foods that can make acid reflux worse include high-fat foods, citrus fruits like oranges and lemons, tomatoes, and spicy or fried foods. It's also best to avoid snacks that are high in fat and sugar, such as fried foods, cakes, and chocolate. Additionally, limiting or avoiding foods like beans, dried fruit, and popcorn can help alleviate symptoms.",
