          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, thanks! I\u2019ll keep eating those. Besides food, are there daily habits that might help lower the chances of having reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some good habits to help someone with stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there are several daily habits that can help lower the chances of having acid reflux. For example, eating smaller, more frequent meals throughout the day can help reduce symptoms. Additionally, avoiding eating immediately before bedtime and propping yourself up in bed can also be beneficial. Furthermore, incorporating light exercise into your daily routine, such as walking or yoga, can aid in digestion and help with weight loss, which can also reduce acid reflux episodes. It's also recommended to chew gum, as it stimulates the salivary glands and can help dilute acid in the esophagus. Lastly, not skipping meals and eating at regular intervals can help prevent gastric problems.",
