          "text": "Yes, weight gain and not exercising can be connected to acid reflux. Gaining weight, even a small amount, can put pressure on the stomach and worsen acid reflux symptoms. On the other hand, regular exercise, especially low-impact activities like walking or yoga, can help alleviate symptoms by reducing pressure on the stomach and promoting better digestion. Since you've gained weight recently due to a lack of exercise, incorporating physical activity into your routine and maintaining a healthy weight may help improve your acid reflux symptoms. Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related Answer Continue Reading Related",
