      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s interesting to know. Thanks for the clear explanation! Are there any ODC medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are there any ODC medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there are several over-the-counter (OTC) medications available for acid reflux. These include antacids, H2 receptor antagonists, and proton pump inhibitors (PPIs). Antacids help neutralize stomach acid, while H2 receptor antagonists reduce acid production in the stomach. PPIs block acid production and are often used for more severe cases of acid reflux. Some examples of OTC medications for acid reflux include Tums, Rolaids, and Prilosec OTC. It's essential to follow the instructions and recommended dosage on the label, and if your symptoms persist or worsen, you should consult with your doctor for further guidance. They can help you determine the best course of treatment for your specific condition. Additionally, lifestyle changes, such as maintaining a healthy weight, eating smaller meals, and avoiding trigger foods, can also help alleviate acid reflux symptoms.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.   (I made the changes as per",
