          "text": "To manage acid reflux, it's best to focus on alkaline foods that can help reduce the acidity of stomach acid. Some good options include ginger, broccoli, cauliflower, mushrooms, green beans, leafy greens, watermelon, root vegetables, ripe bananas, and nuts. On the other hand, it's best to limit or avoid high-fat foods like fried foods, full-fat dairy products, meats with high-fat content, creamy gravies, and sauces. Also, citrus fruits like tomatoes and their juices can trigger acid reflux in many people. It's also a good idea to control your snacking and eating habits, especially before bedtime, as this can help alleviate symptoms. Consider keeping a food diary to track which foods affect you the most. Consult with your doctor for personalized recommendations.  Document ID: Doc1, Doc2, Doc3, Doc4, Doc5",
