    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m curious about acid reflux and foods\u2014what\u2019s generally safe to eat, and what should I stay away from?",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When it comes to acid reflux, it's best to avoid trigger foods that can relax the lower esophageal sphincter or irritate the esophagus. Common culprits include citrus fruits, tomatoes, chocolate, spicy or fatty foods, and caffeine. On the other hand, gentle foods like lean proteins, whole grains, and low-acid fruits like bananas, melons, and apples are often well-tolerated. Since you enjoy a variety of fruits, you might want to try alternatives to citrus fruits or tomatoes, which can trigger acid reflux. It's also a good idea to eat smaller, more frequent meals and avoid lying down after eating to help manage symptoms. As someone who eats dinner late at night, you may want to consider adjusting your meal times to see if it helps alleviate any discomfort.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
