      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yeah, I'm curious about foods for acid reflux. Which ones help, and which should I avoid?",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For acid reflux, it's best to avoid trigger foods that can irritate the esophagus and worsen symptoms. Common culprits include citrus fruits like oranges, grapefruits, and lemons, as well as tomatoes and tomato-based products. Spicy foods, fatty or fried foods, and chocolate can also exacerbate acid reflux. On the other hand, some foods may help alleviate symptoms. Alkaline-rich foods like bananas, melons, and green vegetables can help neutralize stomach acid. Additionally, lean proteins like chicken and fish, and low-fat dairy products like milk and yogurt, may be easier to digest. However, everyone's triggers are different, so it's essential to keep a food diary to track which foods affect you the most. Consult with your doctor or a registered dietitian for personalized advice.  Document the conversation and the answer.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
