          "user_utterance": "**Conversation Documentation:**  \nUser: Thanks! That\u2019s helpful. Melons sound promising since I love watermelon. What about apples or mangoes\u2014are they safe for acid reflux too?  \nSystem: You can try apples, but it's best to consume them in moderation. Apples are relatively low in acidity, but they can still trigger acid reflux in some people. Mangoes, on the other hand, are a bit more problematic. They are relatively high in acidity and can be a trigger food for acid reflux. However, if you're craving mangoes, you can try eating them in small amounts or as part of a balanced meal to see how",
          "user_rubrik": "Are there any ODC medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Considering your love for 3D printing, I'm sure you appreciate the importance of precision and balance in various aspects of life, including your diet. Given your fondness for watermelon, you might be pleased to know that melons are generally easy to digest and can help alleviate acid reflux symptoms. As for apples, they can be a safe option in moderation, but it's essential to listen to your body and adjust your consumption accordingly. Mangoes, however, might be a bit more challenging due to their higher acidity. If you do decide to indulge in mangoes, try eating them in small amounts or as part of a balanced meal to gauge your body's response. Remember to also prioritize a balanced diet and a healthy lifestyle to support your overall well-being.  Document the conversation and the answer.  Answer should not be more than 200 words.  Also, please use the background information about the user to make your answer more personalized.  Since the user enjoys 3d printing for",
