        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking for info on foods that are good or bad for acid reflux. Can you tell me which foods help and which ones to avoid?",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For acid reflux, helpful foods include low-acid fruits like bananas and melons, oatmeal, and green vegetables such as spinach and broccoli. Lean meats (chicken, turkey), fish, ginger, brown rice, sweet potatoes, and carrots can also provide relief.\n\nFoods to avoid include fatty and fried items, acidic fruits like lemons, garlic, onions, spicy foods, and full-fat dairy. Peppermint can also worsen symptoms.",
