      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, that\u2019s a relief because I really like apples and kiwis! Are there lifestyle changes, aside from food, that can improve reflux symptoms?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some good habits to help someone with stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Yes, both apples and kiwis can be suitable for acid reflux. Apples are generally good because they contain alkalizing minerals like calcium, magnesium, and potassium, which help neutralize stomach acid. It's best to choose sweet or red apples, as tart or sour varieties (like Granny Smith) might worsen symptoms. Kiwis are also considered suitable and can help lower acid.",
