      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s a repeat from before\u2014I was hoping for advice on habits, not just food. Can you give a list of good lifestyle habits for acid reflux management?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some good habits to help someone with stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, several lifestyle changes can significantly improve acid reflux symptoms. These include elevating your head during sleep, avoiding eating 2-3 hours before bedtime, and exercising regularly. Managing stress through practices like meditation or yoga is also beneficial. Additionally, avoid smoking, limit alcohol and caffeine, and stay away from carbonated beverages. Eating smaller, more frequent meals, chewing thoroughly, and chewing gum after meals can help. Losing weight may also alleviate symptoms.",
