          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "1. I have gained weight recently because I stopped exercising for the last 6 months.",
            "2. I eat dinner late at night.",
            "3. I want to change my lifestyle."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s really helpful. I tend to eat dinner late at night, so I\u2019ll need to work on that. Is being overweight a big factor in acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does acid reflux happen? Does acid reflux have a reason?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Yes, being overweight is a significant factor in acid reflux. Excess weight, especially around the abdomen, increases pressure on your stomach and the sphincter between your stomach and esophagus. This pressure can force stomach acid back up into the esophagus, worsening reflux symptoms. Studies show that overweight and obese individuals are at a much higher risk for GERD. Losing weight can significantly alleviate these symptoms.",
