          "user_utterance": "Makes sense, I gained weight recently since I stopped exercising. Is it common for acid reflux to start after gaining weight?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does acid reflux happen? Does acid reflux have a reason?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Yes, it is common for acid reflux to start or worsen after gaining weight. Even a moderate weight gain, particularly around the abdomen, can increase pressure on your stomach and the sphincter between your stomach and esophagus, pushing acid back up. Studies show that even small weight gains, not necessarily leading to being overweight, can significantly increase the risk of acid reflux symptoms.",
