      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it. Are there any OTC medications to help with stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are there any ODC medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Several over-the-counter (OTC) medications can help with acid reflux. These include:\n*   **Antacids** like Tums, Rolaids, Mylanta, and Gaviscon, which neutralize stomach acid for quick relief.\n*   **H2-receptor blockers** such as cimetidine (Tagamet HB), famotidine (Pepcid AC), and ranitidine, which reduce acid production.\n*   **Proton Pump Inhibitors (PPIs)** like omeprazole (Prilosec OTC), esomeprazole (Nexium 24HR), and lansoprazole (Prevacid 24 HR), which block acid production more strongly.\n*   **Alginates** (e.g., Gaviscon) form a protective barrier.",
          "citations": {
