      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it, I\u2019ll try eating earlier and maybe prop up my bed. Is acid reflux only related to food or could things like weight or stress make it worse too?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does acid reflux happen? Does acid reflux have a reason?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "Yes, acid reflux isn't only about food. Both weight and stress can significantly worsen it. Being overweight or obese increases abdominal pressure, which can push stomach acid into the esophagus. Stress can also exacerbate symptoms by affecting digestion, potentially increasing stomach acid, or making you more sensitive to reflux pain. Other factors like certain medications or smoking can also play a role.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0023-27-00769:2": 0.8256617784500122,
            "clueweb22-en0011-42-03246:12": 0.7425894141197205,
            "clueweb22-en0003-88-05119:5": 0.7325759530067444,
