        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s super helpful! I eat a lot of apples and just started loving mangoes after my Brazil trip. Are there any drinks that help with reflux, or should most drinks be avoided?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some good habits to help someone with stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "For acid reflux, good drink options include water, caffeine-free herbal teas, low-fat or plant-based milks, smoothies, and coconut water. Low-acid fruit juices like carrot, aloe vera, beet, watermelon, spinach, cucumber, or pear are also beneficial.\n\nDrinks to limit or avoid include carbonated beverages, highly caffeinated drinks (like coffee or black tea), and alcohol. Acidic juices, such as citrus and pineapple, should generally be avoided; while apple fruit is good, apple juice can be acidic for some.",
