      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! That\u2019s interesting about apple juice\u2014didn\u2019t realize it could be tough for some people. I\u2019m trying to change up my evening routines. What are some good habits to help someone with stomach acid reflux, especially at night? I tend to eat dinner pretty late.",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some good habits to help someone with stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To manage acid reflux in the evening, especially with late dinners, aim to eat at least 2-4 hours before bed. After dinner, stay upright for 2-3 hours; avoid lying down or vigorous exercise. Elevate the head of your bed by 6 inches and try sleeping on your left side. Opt for smaller evening meals and avoid common triggers like fatty, spicy, or acidic foods, chocolate, caffeine, and alcohol. Relaxation techniques can also help.",
