          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting\u2014I\u2019ve actually gained a bit of weight since I stopped exercising. That might be a factor for me. Are there over-the-counter medications that help with acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are there any ODC medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Over-the-counter medications for acid reflux include antacids like Tums, Maalox, Mylanta, and Rolaids, which provide quick relief by neutralizing stomach acid. Alginates, such as Gaviscon, form a protective barrier.\n\nYou can also find H2-blockers like famotidine (Pepcid AC) and cimetidine (Tagamet HB), which reduce acid production, and proton pump inhibitors (PPIs) such as omeprazole (Prilosec OTC) and lansoprazole (Prevacid 24 HR), which block acid production and help heal the esophagus.",
          "citations": {
