      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Makes sense, thanks. Are there any OTC medications that help with acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are there any ODC medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For acid reflux, several over-the-counter (OTC) medications can help. These include:\n\n*   **Antacids** (e.g., Tums, Rolaids, Mylanta, Gaviscon) which quickly neutralize stomach acid for temporary relief.\n*   **H2 Blockers** (e.g., Pepcid AC/famotidine, Tagamet HB/cimetidine) which reduce acid production.\n*   **Proton Pump Inhibitors (PPIs)** (e.g., Prilosec OTC/omeprazole, Prevacid 24 HR/lansoprazole) which block acid production and can help heal the esophagus.",
