      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Oh, I\u2019ve seen Tums around. How do these medications actually work to stop the reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "How do medication for stomach acid reflux work?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Antacids like Tums work by directly neutralizing existing stomach acid. H2 blockers reduce acid production by blocking histamine receptors in your stomach that trigger acid release. Proton Pump Inhibitors (PPIs) are stronger, working by shutting down the \"pumps\" responsible for secreting acid into your stomach, significantly reducing acid production.",
          "citations": {
