          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm looking for foods that are good or bad for acid reflux. Any tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For acid reflux, good foods include low-acid fruits (bananas, melons, apples), most vegetables (broccoli, leafy greens, sweet potatoes), lean proteins (skinless chicken, turkey, fish, egg whites), and whole grains (oatmeal, brown rice). Opt for low-fat dairy and high-fiber foods.\n\nAvoid high-fat foods (fried foods, fatty meats), acidic fruits (citrus, tomatoes, pineapple), spicy foods, onions, garlic, caffeine, alcohol, and mint.\n\nTips include eating smaller portions, cooking with little oil, and avoiding lying down immediately after meals.",
