      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s super helpful. I do tend to eat dinner pretty late, so maybe I should change that. Does weight gain affect acid reflux too?",
          "user_rubrik": "Why does acid reflux happen? Does acid reflux have a reason?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Yes, weight gain significantly affects acid reflux. Excess body fat, especially around the abdomen, increases pressure on your stomach and the sphincter between your stomach and esophagus, which can cause acid to rise. Even small or moderate weight gain can increase your risk of acid reflux symptoms, and losing weight is often an effective strategy to reduce or eliminate them.",
