          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Hi! I wanted to know which foods are good for dealing with acid reflux, and which ones should I avoid.",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For acid reflux, focus on low-acid, low-fat, and high-fiber foods. Good options include bananas, melons, apples, leafy greens, carrots, broccoli, oatmeal, brown rice, whole-grain breads, lean chicken/turkey, and lean fish. Water and almond milk are beneficial.\n\nAvoid high-fat/fried foods, acidic items (citrus, tomatoes), spicy foods, peppermint, spearmint, garlic, raw onions, and high-fat dairy.",
