        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it, thanks for breaking that down. Are there any ODC medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Are there any ODC medications for stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there are several over-the-counter (OTC) medications for stomach acid reflux. These include:\n\n*   **Antacids** (e.g., Tums, Rolaids, Mylanta, Gaviscon) neutralize stomach acid for quick relief.\n*   **H2 blockers** (e.g., famotidine like Pepcid AC, cimetidine like Tagamet HB) reduce acid production.\n*   **Proton Pump Inhibitors (PPIs)** (e.g., omeprazole like Prilosec OTC, lansoprazole like Prevacid 24 HR) block acid production and can help heal the esophagus.",
          "citations": {
