  {
    "runtag": "uva-gpt5-bm25-debertav3-gpt5mini-nopersonal",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "1-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking to find out which foods are good or bad for acid reflux. Any suggestions?",
          "user_rubrik": "What  food is good for stomach acid reflux and some that I should avoid?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Good choices - Vegetables (especially green ones): broccoli, asparagus, leafy greens, peas, cucumbers, Brussels sprouts \u2014 most veggies help and are low in fat. - High-fiber foods: whole grains, legumes, fruits (non\u2011citrus), and vegetables \u2014 fiber helps digestion and reduces reflux. - Lean proteins and seafood, nuts, seeds \u2014 choose lower\u2011fat options. - A Mediterranean-style pattern (more fish, vegetables, whole grains; fewer fatty/processed meats) is often helpful.  Foods to avoid or limit - High\u2011fat and fried foods (they relax the lower esophageal sphincter and slow emptying). - Spicy foods, citrus fruits, tomatoes and tomato products. - Onions and garlic (common triggers for many people). - Caffeine (coffee), alcohol, peppermint/mint, and carbonated beverages. - High\u2011fat dairy (use low\u2011fat choices if tolerated).  Practical tips - Avoid saut\u00e9ing in lots of butter or margarine; bake, grill, steam instead. - Increase fiber gradually and track your personal triggers \u2014 people vary, so keep a food diary to find what affects you.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0021-74-19197:1": 33.871299743652344,
