      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice, thanks! Which fruits specifically count as non-citrus and are usually safe for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some fruits good for acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Good choices (commonly well tolerated) - Bananas - Apples (peeled if raw onions/skin bother you) - Pears - Melons: watermelon, cantaloupe, honeydew - Peaches and nectarines - Mango and papaya (papaya can aid digestion) - Berries in moderation: blueberries, strawberries, raspberries - Guava (often tolerated)  Fruits to avoid or limit - Citrus: oranges, lemons, limes, grapefruit - Pineapple and tomato products - Cranberry and other tart fruit juices  Quick tips - Eat whole fruit rather than juices (juices are more acidic/concentrated). - Choose ripe fruit (less acidic) and avoid large portions at once. - Keep a simple food diary \u2014 individual triggers vary, so track what bothers you and adjust.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0002-19-16904:6": 23.25550079345703,
