          "text": "Good question \u2014 small diet and habit changes can make a big difference.  Foods to avoid (common triggers) - Fried, greasy, high\u2011fat foods and large servings of red meat (stay away from fatty cuts) - Chocolate, peppermint/spearmint, coffee/caffeinated drinks, alcohol - Citrus, tomato and tomato sauces, carbonated drinks, spicy/very oniony or garlicky meals  Foods to eat more of - Lean proteins: fish, skinless poultry, legumes/beans, tofu - High\u2011fiber whole grains and veggies: oatmeal, brown rice, sweet potato, broccoli, leafy greens - Non\u2011citrus fruits: apples, watermelon, kiwi; moderate avocado/healthy fats (olive oil, walnuts) - Fermented foods with probiotics: yogurt, kefir, miso, sauerkraut (may help digestion) - Nuts (almonds) and B\u2011vitamin/calcium sources like spinach and fortified cereals  Lifestyle tips - Avoid overeating; have smaller, frequent meals - Don\u2019t eat within 2\u20133 hours of lying down (especially since you eat late) - Eat slowly, stay hydrated, lose excess weight, avoid smoking and limit alcohol  If symptoms persist or worsen, see your provider for testing or meds.",
