          "text": "Yes \u2014 for most people bananas are a reflux-friendly choice. They're low-acid, high in fiber and potassium, and act like a gentle natural antacid. Ripe bananas are easiest on the stomach.  A few practical tips: - Pair a banana with a protein (low\u2011fat yogurt, kefir, or a spoon of almond/peanut butter) to boost protein and keep you full.   - If dairy bothers you, try plant-based yogurt or just the banana.   - Pay attention to your own reaction \u2014 a small number of people find bananas trigger their GERD, so avoid if you notice symptoms after eating them.   - Keep portion sizes moderate and don\u2019t lie down right after eating (try to stop eating 2\u20133 hours before bed).  If reflux persists despite these changes, check with your provider.",
