          "text": "Good choices \u2014 and yes, there are some drinks to avoid and better swaps.  Drinks to avoid or limit - Carbonated/sparkling water and sodas (they cause burping/gastric distention and can worsen reflux) - Citrus juices (orange, grapefruit, lemon/lime) and very tart fruit juices - Coffee and other caffeinated drinks (tea, some colas) \u2014 they can relax the LES; decaf may be easier on you - Alcohol and chocolate drinks - Sports drinks with citric acid - Flavored waters that are acidic  Better options - Plain water (or alkaline water for some people) - Caffeine\u2011free herbal teas (avoid peppermint/spearmint) \u2014 chamomile, licorice, slippery elm - Low\u2011fat milk or plant milks (almond, coconut) - Smoothies made with non\u2011citrus fruits and yogurt/kefir  Practical tip: avoid drinking large amounts right before bed \u2014 stop fluids 2\u20133 hours before lying down if possible. If symptoms persist, see your provider.",
